2b00f1dc (2572 1793703464500 "guenchi" (("4gm4c2jr" . 3240) ("w5vbequy" . 14982)) (put ((kind . section) (title . "landing f421") (src . "Scheme definers, locate whole, context titles, edit-sync records\n\nFive readings from a consumer's first weeks on 1.3.3, each with a\nred-first row.\n\nThe Scheme language entries (scheme and chez) gain definition heads for\ndefine-checked, define-record-type in both spellings,\ndefine-condition-type, define-values (the first name),\ndefine-enumeration, define-integrable in both spellings and\ndefine-structure, so split-suggest cuts before each and names it, and\nnames, uses and context see their definitions; before, every such form\nrode in the preceding define's block under that define's name.\n\nlocate with no range answers every block the file is made of, in file\norder, zero-length blocks included, each with its own span; before it\nanswered only its usage line, though README marked the ranges optional.\n\ncontext's entry heads carry the block's name as the title when it has\nno title (a symbol or a string as its text, a list by its first element,\nelse \"\"); a code block's name is read from the record the request\nalready holds, so the store is still read in one place.\n\nedit-sync records what it wrote: a sync that completes its plan rewrites\nthe sidecar as a fresh export of the same cut would record the synced\ndirectory, pristine copies first and the sidecar last, so a second sync\nof the same export directory is not refused draft-changed, an undone add\nis discarded, and a sync that died before the rename is retried from\nthe old sidecar.\n\nA runner-language eval with --working answers the draft table as the\nScheme path does, (id . version) per draft; it no longer embeds each\ndraft's bytes.\n\nTests: test/scheme-definers.sc (new, 19 rows, with a synthetic consumer\nfile of the reading's shape), locate 36 rows, edit-tools 78 rows,\neval-lang 151 rows; rows-baseline updated.\n") (parent . root) (ord . 618))))
